                <pb facs="0811" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4981: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Viborg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Imbrie</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Viborg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-07"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 8, 1:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>73. Three British ships are now unloading artillery, tanks and other munitions at
                    Reval for the use of the Russian White forces in Estonia. September 1st has been
                    set as a tentative date when the Russian Whites, with the support of the British
                    Baltic Fleet, will attempt a drive against Petrograd. If this drive is
                    unsuccessful the Whites have no hope of occupying the city before summer of
                    1920. At present Bolsheviks have the advantage on this front and have just
                    recaptured [Yamburg?].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Imbrie</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
